  "claim": "A mythical forest creature that is seductive and from northern Sweden has the same being as the divine figure Huld.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Skogsrå. Sentence: The skogsrå , (Forest Rå), \"Skogsfrun\" (The Mistress of the Forest), \"Skogssnuvan\", \"Skogsnymfen\" (Forest Nymph), \"Råndan\" (the Rå) or \"huldra\", was a mythical creature of the forest, or Rå, in Swedish folklore.\nPage: Hulder. Sentence: A hulder is a seductive forest creature found in Scandinavian folklore.\nPage: Hulder. Sentence: She is known as the skogsrå \"forest spirit\" or Tallemaja \"pine tree Mary\" in Swedish folklore, and ulda in Sámi folklore.\nPage: Hulder. Sentence: Her name suggests that she is originally the same being as the völva divine figure Huld and the German Holda.",
