        "original_id": "7546619f-388b-5a19-9b0f-f311a06f0511",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: skogsrå, hulder, huldra, rå\n- Topics: Scandinavian folklore, Swedish folklore, Sámi folklore, mythological beings\n\nFacts:\n- In Swedish folklore, the skogsrå was a mythical forest being identified as a type of rå.\n- In Swedish folklore, the skogsrå was also called Skogsfrun, Skogssnuvan, Skogsnymfen, Råndan, and huldra.\n- In Scandinavian folklore, a hulder is a seductive forest creature.\n- In Swedish folklore, the hulder is known as the skogsrå and as Tallemaja.\n- In Sámi folklore, the hulder is known as ulda.\n- The hulder’s name suggests a shared original identity with the divine figure Huld and the German Holda.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
